From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xianzhu Wang <wangxianzhu@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:01:07 -0700
Subject: [HiC] Supress paint invalidation of spell/grammar markers in canvas
 subtree

Though we supress paint of spell/grammer markers in canvas subtree,
previously we still invalidate paint of them, causing user dictionary
leaks through the html-in-canvas API.

Now suppress paint invalidations of them to prevent the leak.

In document_marker_controller.cc, InvalidateVisualOverflowForNode is
fold into InvalidatePaintForNode. This simplifies code to suppress
paint invalidation for spell/grammer markers. That could cause a few
more redundant paint invalidation calls in some cases but the cost
is trivial, and that won't cause any extra paint invalidation.

Fixed: 563359033
Change-Id: I20f15ba16eaa307294d4d8e45935293ae6d72a9a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8489082
Reviewed-by: Stefan Zager <szager@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Xianzhu Wang <wangxianzhu@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1710351}

